{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Howl.</b> The sense: they raise their voice in public." "<b>For from the north smoke comes.</b> It is the king of Assyria, but the correct interpretation is that it is Nebuchadnezzar, and the proof: for YHWH has founded Zion." "<b>and none isolated.</b> From the root בדד." "<b>in his appointed times.</b> In his palaces the smoke has entered, and no man can sit, even alone, in his house."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:53.064954669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}